# package.json's format/format:check scripts already scope to **/*.{js,mjs},
# so index.html (a .html file whose logic happens to live in an inline
# <script>) is never matched by that glob -- this entry is belt-and-suspenders
# documentation of WHY, in case the scripts' glob is ever loosened to "."
# later: prettier's HTML formatter reformats the entire file (re-indents
# <head>, expands hand-written single-line CSS rules in the <style> block
# onto multiple lines, converts self-closing tag style, etc.) -- verified by
# actually running `prettier --write` against a scratch copy: a ~4,300-line
# diff on a 1,660-line file. Forcing that through would swamp and mask real
# code changes under near-total whitespace/tag-style churn -- exactly the
# risk docs/CODE_STANDARDS.md's own "ratchet, not a rewrite" reasoning (see
# QUALITY_STANDARD.md §8) warns against. Formatting index.html is a real,
# worthwhile follow-up -- just as its own clearly-isolated, reviewable change.
index.html
